  "cli_result_text": "Submitted. Summary of the chain for the ticket:\n\n1. **`pkg/registry/core/rest/storage_core.go`** \u2014 `legacyProvider.PostStartHook()` registers `start-service-ip-repair-controllers`. It runs the cluster-IP and node-port repair controllers, waits up to 1 minute for both to report `onFirstSuccess()`, and on timeout returns `goerrors.New(\"unable to perform initial IP and Port allocation check\")` \u2014 the exact string in the ticket.\n2. **`staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/server/hooks.go`** \u2014 `runPostStartHook` treats any non-nil hook error as fatal (`klog.Fatalf(\"PostStartHook %q failed: %v\", ...)`), which kills the apiserver process; and until `done` is closed, `postStartHookHealthz.Check` keeps returning `errHookNotFinished`, which is what feeds the `readyz` handler's `poststarthook/start-service-ip-repair-controllers` line.\n3. **`pkg/registry/core/service/ipallocator/controller/repairip.go`** \u2014 `RepairIPAddress.doRunOnce`/`syncService` creates/updates `networking.k8s.io/v1beta1.IPAddress` objects via the loopback client as part of its first reconcile pass, which must succeed before `onFirstSuccess()` fires.\n4. **`staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/admission/plugin/policy/generic/plugin.go`** + **`validating/plugin.go`** \u2014 the ValidatingAdmissionPolicy generic admission plugin is unconditionally enabled (`p.SetEnabled(true)`) and its `Dispatch` rejects *every* write with `admission.NewForbidden(a, fmt.Errorf(\"not yet ready to handle request\"))` until its own namespace/policy-source informers have synced (`WaitForReady()`), independent of whether any policy is actually configured.\n\n**The race**: during the mixed-version rolling upgrade window, the repair controller's very first IPAddress write can land before the admission plugin's own cache sync completes, producing `ipaddresses.networking.k8s.io \"...\" is forbidden: not yet ready to handle request`. `doRunOnce`/`syncService` returns that error, `onFirstSuccess` is never called, the 1-minute timer in the PostStartHook fires, the hook returns the allocation-check error, `klog.Fatalf` kills the process, and until that point `/readyz` fails on `informer-sync` + the poststarthook check. It self-heals once all nodes are on the same version because the timing skew that causes the two informer-sync races to overlap goes away.",
